(4894960, 708983, 42198, '<td valign="top">I don''t think it was just the foil background that hurt the score. A few other observations;<br/> <br/>- Centered composition. In most cases centering the subject looks boring. Try a rule-of-thirds composition<br/> <br/>- Boring subject. To be honest, there''s not much you could do to make this item look interesting. It looks like something you just found in a desk drawer 5 minutes before the submission time. It just doesn''t hold my interest or tell any sort of story.<br/> <br/>- Subject too small in frame. Try moving in closer to the subject, or at least cropping out all that empty space around it.<br/> <br/>As far as backdrops go, try using a large sheet of white or coloured paper. For example;<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=560267" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/716/120/560267.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/716/120/560267.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/716/120/560267.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>That''s a sheet of red card I bought in Easons. It doesn''t detract from the subject, but creates a contrasting colour for the background. Just be careful with your lighting when using white backdrops, you want to avoid weird shadows appearing.</td>', 'I don''t think it was just the foil background that hurt the score. A few other observations; - Centered composition. In most cases centering the subject looks boring. Try a rule-of-thirds composition - Boring subject. To be honest, there''s not much you could do to make this item look interesting. It looks like something you just found in a desk drawer 5 minutes before the submission time. It just doesn''t hold my interest or tell any sort of story. - Subject too small in frame. Try moving in closer to the subject, or at least cropping out all that empty space around it. As far as backdrops go, try using a large sheet of white or coloured paper. For example;   That''s a sheet of red card I bought in Easons. It doesn''t detract from the subject, but creates a contrasting colour for the background. Just be careful with your lighting when using white backdrops, you want to avoid weird shadows appearing.', '2008-08-18 08:13:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(4894962, 708770, 67152, '<td valign="top">I am really quite surprised this did not finish higher.  I love the humor in the facial expression, the strong contrast used, the choice of objects to be held (the cat is what seals it for me).  Great work again..one of my favorites for the top spot.</td>', 'I am really quite surprised this did not finish higher.  I love the humor in the facial expression, the strong contrast used, the choice of objects to be held (the cat is what seals it for me).  Great work again..one of my favorites for the top spot.', '2008-08-18 08:15:28.000000', NULL, 0),
