(4895844, 708482, 97166, '<td valign="top">Following up on my comment. <br/>I see that you shot this in ISO 1000, which would account for the noise in the black of your outfit.<br/> <br/>Interesting choice. Was it accidental or purposely? I''m interested in learning which, and why</td>', 'Following up on my comment. I see that you shot this in ISO 1000, which would account for the noise in the black of your outfit. Interesting choice. Was it accidental or purposely? I''m interested in learning which, and why', '2008-08-18 17:02:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(4895854, 708815, 97166, '<td valign="top">Following up on my comment.<br/> <br/>I thought this would place higher too, and when I got to page 2 and still didn''t see this, I was a little shocked. It was an 8 from me, but I guess you can''t win them all.<br/> <br/>Brad has some interesting points.  I didn''t notice the finger creases myself, but it seems a couple of people did. He''s right though, now that I see them, it''s almost all I see. <br/> <br/>Anway, I like this shot, and it was one of my highest scoring, so be proud, no matter where it ended up.</td>', 'Following up on my comment. I thought this would place higher too, and when I got to page 2 and still didn''t see this, I was a little shocked. It was an 8 from me, but I guess you can''t win them all. Brad has some interesting points.  I didn''t notice the finger creases myself, but it seems a couple of people did. He''s right though, now that I see them, it''s almost all I see.  Anway, I like this shot, and it was one of my highest scoring, so be proud, no matter where it ended up.', '2008-08-18 17:09:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(4895858, 708207, 97166, '<td valign="top">Following up on my comment:<br/> <br/>Well, congrats on finishing fairly high.  I hope you weren''t too offended by my comment, but the thought sticks with me. I can only imagine where this would have finished in a challenge called "Perspective"!</td>', 'Following up on my comment: Well, congrats on finishing fairly high.  I hope you weren''t too offended by my comment, but the thought sticks with me. I can only imagine where this would have finished in a challenge called "Perspective"!', '2008-08-18 17:12:19.000000', NULL, 0),
