(4900059, 709122, 23913, '<td valign="top">Just so you know, i know of no musician who will wear a fender strap with a fender T (save maybe eric clapton, and they pay him).<br/>Also I would point out the idea of raising the camera up and shooting down (@ about the same degree you shot up) on this pose. This would take away the up the nose view we all have, it would bring your face more to the top 3rds convergence point (using the rule is good most always), lastly it would take away the feel as though you have just been given the last blow in a Rocky movie.<br/> <br/>The hair is cool it works really well but its cut off, i think i''ve supported my point well enough but swinging the camera up to more of a top down would help this fact as well.<br/> <br/>very last i will mention that this is DPC so its all just a bunch of punk photo junkies, and semi pros (myself included) none of this needs to be done or taken to heart. Try a reshoot never the less just to see the difference, and for goodness sakes loose the fender shirt or get paid to wear it.<br/> <br/>-b</td>', 'Just so you know, i know of no musician who will wear a fender strap with a fender T (save maybe eric clapton, and they pay him).Also I would point out the idea of raising the camera up and shooting down (@ about the same degree you shot up) on this pose. This would take away the up the nose view we all have, it would bring your face more to the top 3rds convergence point (using the rule is good most always), lastly it would take away the feel as though you have just been given the last blow in a Rocky movie. The hair is cool it works really well but its cut off, i think i''ve supported my point well enough but swinging the camera up to more of a top down would help this fact as well. very last i will mention that this is DPC so its all just a bunch of punk photo junkies, and semi pros (myself included) none of this needs to be done or taken to heart. Try a reshoot never the less just to see the difference, and for goodness sakes loose the fender shirt or get paid to wear it. -b', '2008-08-20 10:57:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(4900566, 709121, 3548, '<td valign="top">Who you are and what you are is not defined by what you do. <br/>Doing is not Being and Being is not Doing. While they are related, they are not the same. It is the great American fallacy. It is also what is an integral part of what is the collective neurosis that has led to and created the Crisis that we are in -- and in denial about.<br/> <br/>When we bring Doing to Being and our Being into Doing then we have integrity and cogency in both. Otherwise we create conflict and dissonance in our selves, our lives and our relationships. <br/> <br/>In our obsessive-compulsive, work addicted world and lives, we have sacrificed our selves and our souls to an end we can never reach by the very approach we are taking. You, sir, have been given the time and opportunity to re-think, re-orient and re-create your self and your life. Hopefully, you''ll utilize this time in that manner.<br/> <br/>When you learn to do nothing and to be nobody you will then become useful to the universe.<br/> <br/>In Spirit.<br/>A fellow hermit.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-08-20 16:20:00.</i></td>', 'Who you are and what you are is not defined by what you do. Doing is not Being and Being is not Doing. While they are related, they are not the same. It is the great American fallacy. It is also what is an integral part of what is the collective neurosis that has led to and created the Crisis that we are in -- and in denial about. When we bring Doing to Being and our Being into Doing then we have integrity and cogency in both. Otherwise we create conflict and dissonance in our selves, our lives and our relationships.  In our obsessive-compulsive, work addicted world and lives, we have sacrificed our selves and our souls to an end we can never reach by the very approach we are taking. You, sir, have been given the time and opportunity to re-think, re-orient and re-create your self and your life. Hopefully, you''ll utilize this time in that manner. When you learn to do nothing and to be nobody you will then become useful to the universe. In Spirit.A fellow hermit.', '2008-08-20 15:01:17.000000', '2008-08-20 17:20:00.000000', 0),
