(5107798, 709101, 74559, '<td valign="top">Wow, fantastic image! Love the lighting, your expression, vivid color and detail, everything is perfect!</td>', 'Wow, fantastic image! Love the lighting, your expression, vivid color and detail, everything is perfect!', '2008-12-05 02:03:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(5109141, 709101, 87808, '<td valign="top">SO not fair, every time i see this shot, I go weak at the knees!!!</td>', 'SO not fair, every time i see this shot, I go weak at the knees!!!', '2008-12-05 11:36:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(5152945, 708120, 60195, '<td valign="top">I really like this image (for several reasons).  First, the composition is great - as is the subject.  Who can resist a cute, furry little chick like that? (<i><b>very</b></i> DPC friendly).  <br/>A couple of things caught my eye on the technicals... things that IMO would have made this really pop:<pre>    1. For a cleaner look - you might try cloning out the small dust spots on the mirror<br/>    2. You mention this was f/5.6, so I can only assume that you blurred the background in software <br/>       (it looks razor thin - f/1.8ish).  While I''m normally a HUGE fan of super shallow DoF, I actually <br/>       think this would''ve benefitted from a bit <i>more</i> depth. The only thing in focus is the very front edge <br/>       of the chick.  Maybe try taking it back to the first shell (?)<br/>    3. Just a bit lacking in contrast - this would''ve really popped off of the screen with a bit more.</pre>Again - stellar image, with a lot of potential to have ribboned. :O)<br/></td>', 'I really like this image (for several reasons).  First, the composition is great - as is the subject.  Who can resist a cute, furry little chick like that? (very DPC friendly).  A couple of things caught my eye on the technicals... things that IMO would have made this really pop:    1. For a cleaner look - you might try cloning out the small dust spots on the mirror    2. You mention this was f/5.6, so I can only assume that you blurred the background in software        (it looks razor thin - f/1.8ish).  While I''m normally a HUGE fan of super shallow DoF, I actually        think this would''ve benefitted from a bit more depth. The only thing in focus is the very front edge        of the chick.  Maybe try taking it back to the first shell (?)    3. Just a bit lacking in contrast - this would''ve really popped off of the screen with a bit more.Again - stellar image, with a lot of potential to have ribboned. :O)', '2008-12-27 04:22:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(5154160, 708120, 46177, '<td valign="top">Adorable, I like the soft textures of the feathers and the subdued colours. The dof is excellent.</td>', 'Adorable, I like the soft textures of the feathers and the subdued colours. The dof is excellent.', '2008-12-27 21:54:43.000000', NULL, 0),
